From 72f8e148173ae110f4b7dd38af22358c2af36439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:48:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] piano: SC8541 switched-capacitor stage and direct charging
 (#27)

* dt-bindings: power: supply: add the Southchip SC8541 charger

The SC8541 is a single-cell 2:1 switched-capacitor direct charger with
an I2C interface, used with USB PD PPS sources.  Add its binding and
the "southchip" vendor prefix.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* power: supply: add a Southchip SC8541 charger driver

The SC8541 is the 2:1 switched-capacitor stage of the Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro
(piano), on the fuel gauge I2C bus at 0x6a.  Stock drives it from its
own fast charging strategy; there is no public datasheet beyond a
two-page brief.  The register layout used here, which follows the TI
bq25960, comes from the stock sc8541.ko (GPL-2.0, binary only): device
id 0x41 at 0x22, CHG_EN and EN_BYPASS in 0x0f, the protection
thresholds and their offsets (battery OVP 3840 + 10 mV per step, bus
OVP 7000 + 50 mV, bus OCP 1000 + 250 mA) and the ADC channels and
scales.  On the device the registers left by stock read back as the
stock device tree values under these formulas (4800 mV, 4600 mV,
13000 mV, 7000 mA, VAC OVP 14 V), and the ADC bus and battery voltages
agree with the PMIC and the fuel gauges within 1 %.

The driver runs no algorithm.  It registers a power supply whose
"online" property enables switching: every enable first programs the
battery OVP to 4300 mV (stock: 4800), the bus OVP to 11 V and the bus
OCP to the input current limit (default 3.5 A; the caller may set
1-7 A through "input_current_limit", which also takes effect at once)
and starts the ADC, checking each of those writes by reading it back,
and switching turns itself off unless "online" is written again within
3 s, so a caller that stops running cannot leave it switching.

CHG_EN reads back as set only some time after it is written (stock
checks it 300 ms later).  An early version read it straight back,
took the stale 0 for a refusal and "stopped" with a read-modify-write
that wrote nothing, so the stage started anyway.  CHG_EN is therefore
always written whatever it reads, the caller checks it at its next
poll, and every stop is checked again 500 ms later and repeated while
the chip still reports switching; unbind, shutdown and suspend stop,
wait 500 ms and stop again.

Probe only reads the chip (and stops it if it finds it switching).  The
input OVP gate, the VAC OVP threshold and the register reset bit are
never written, so the buck charger input is left as the bootloader set
it up.  debugfs dumps the registers and the ADC channels, and can start
the ADC alone.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: opt-in direct charging through the SC8541 stage

Stock reaches its 67 W through a PPS source and the SC8541 2:1
switched-capacitor stage, with the buck charger running alongside
(mca_strategy_quickchg, pmic_single_cp_chg); the buck charger alone
stops at about 22 W of input and 3 A into the battery.

Add cp_charge (off by default; needs hv_charge and charge_current):
once a PD source with a PPS APDO that reaches past 8.5 V sits at 9 V
on the buck charger, with both cells at 3.5-4.0 V and 15-38 degC and
the stage idle, the buck charger is held at 500 mA, the stage's bus
over-current protection is set 1 A above the target (at most 6 A) and
the source is asked for twice the battery voltage plus 300 mV, as
stock's open path does.  The stage is then enabled and the voltage
raised 40 mV per 500 ms poll until it carries current, and from there
regulated in 20 mV steps so the bus current stays within 200 mA below
cp_ibus_max (default 2000 mA, at most 4800 mA and 700 mA below what the
source offers, which is asked for up to 5 A) and the battery current
of both gauges below cp_ibat_max (default 5000 mA, at most 8000 mA;
4000 mA below 18 degC).  Stock allows 8 A up to 4.15 V at 18-48 degC
without FFC and 12.4 A with it.

Direct charging ends, back to 9 V on the buck charger until the source
is detached, at a cell voltage of 4100 mV, a battery temperature above
40 degC, a stage die temperature above 80 degC, a bus voltage at the
stage more than 1.2 V above twice the battery voltage (the source may
be asked for up to 2 V above, for the cable drop), a bus current 500 mA
or a battery current 1000 mA above its limit, less than 300 mA of bus
current for 3 s, the stage turning itself off (a protection), any read
or request failure, an adapter authentication, detach, an ADSP restart
or unbind.  The stage also turns itself off when it is not kicked for
3 s.

The write path accepts PPS requests of 6.0-10.0 V at up to 5 A only
with cp_charge set.

On the device, from a PPS power bank with a 5-11 V 3 A APDO: 2 A of
bus current gave 3.8 A into the battery against 3.0 A from the buck
charger alone, the stage die at 40.5 degC and the cells at 33 degC;
unbind and detach stopped the stage.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: hold 9 V back while the adapter authenticates

With mipps_auth set, the 9 V request went out within 30 ms of
xiaomi-mipps-auth starting on attach.  The source's voltage change
then ran across the identity exchange: the adapter SVID and id stayed
0 and the authentication gave up, every time, with the plug either way
round.  The existing hold-off only covers the time verify_process is
set, which the tool does a moment too late.

Wait MCA_HV_AUTH_WAIT_MS (15 s) after attach before asking for 9 V
when mipps_auth is set; a source that does not authenticate gets 9 V
that much later.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: start direct charging after the authentication reset

Once authenticated, a Xiaomi adapter stays at 5 V, the ADSP refuses
further PD requests (retcode 512) and the adapter resets itself about
15 s later, with or without anything asked of it.  Asking for 9 V in
that window, or starting direct charging, met the refusal and the
reset; and the ADSP keeps pd_verifed and the UVDM state across
attaches, so it says nothing about the current attach.

Track the authentication from xiaomi-mipps-auth writing pd_verifed:
leave the adapter alone until its reset (MCA_AUTH_RESET_WAIT_MS at
most), then start direct charging from 5 V by PPS without asking for
9 V first, as stock does.  Being away for longer than a reset takes
ends it.  The buck path still runs whenever direct charging does not
start.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: direct charging from a verified adapter that does not reset

A Xiaomi adapter, unlike the MiPPS power bank tested before, does not
reset itself after the authentication.  It stays at 5 V while the
charger firmware, once the adapter is verified, lists its full APDO
(3.6-11 V 6 A for the 120 W adapter).  Direct charging after the
authentication waited for that reset (a new attach after auth_at), so
it never started.

Also start it, once the reset wait is over, when the charger firmware
reports the adapter verified (0x21010).  Tested with a Xiaomi 120 W
adapter at cp_ibus_max 2000/3000/4000: PPS from 5 V accepted, up to
bus 8.43 V 3.84 A plus the buck charger, 6.5 A into the battery, stage
58.5 degC.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: direct charging limits from the stock battery tables

Direct charging ran with fixed limits: 5 A into the battery (4 A below
18 degC), only below 38 degC and 4.1 V, the bus current set by hand and
no reaction to the stage heating up, which at 4 A on the bus warmed by
about 1 degC/s and reached 58.5 degC within half a minute.

Follow stock (mca_strategy_quickchg, batt_para_lwn and
normal_volt_para18_35, no FFC as the charger firmware floats at
4350 mV), within a narrower window:

  - battery: 8 A, 7.23 A from 4150 mV, 4.5 A below 18 degC and from
    40 degC (back to full below 38 degC); runs 15-45 degC and up to
    4200 mV, starts below 38 degC and 4100 mV;
  - bus: cp_ibus_max (default now 4000) up to 5000 mA (stock
    div_max_curr) from a verified Xiaomi adapter, 4100 mA (stock
    third_pps_ibus_max) from other PPS sources, and asks up to 6 A of
    the source;
  - stage: from 70 degC the bus target drops 200 mA a poll down to
    1 A, and comes back by 50 mA a poll below 65 degC; 80 degC still
    leaves;
  - regulation steps down in proportion to the excess (up to 200 mV),
    and a lowered battery limit trips only after 5 s, so a limit
    stepping down is regulated to rather than ending the session.

Also compare the currents signed: a negative reading against an
unsigned limit counted as far above it.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: buck charger in parallel with direct charging

Direct charging held the buck charger at 500 mA, so the stage carried
nearly all of the battery current and its heat.  Stock
(strategy_quickchg_pmic_single_cp_charging, pmic_single_cp_chg) lets
the buck charger carry part of it: FCC 4000/3000/2000/1000 mA by the
target battery current and the stage's bus current, input FCC / 2
+ 500, while the battery is below 4480 mV.

Without FFC the battery limit stays within 8 A, which reaches stock's
5000 mA / 2700 mA row: above 2700 mA on the stage's bus, with more
than 5 A asked of the battery, set the buck charger to FCC 2000 and
input 1500 mA (back below 2400 mA), from a source that offers enough
for both.  The bus target is lowered by the buck charger's input, and
the request steps down by its expected share when it comes in.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: hold the battery limit through the stage's bus current

Tested with the Xiaomi 120 W adapter at cp_ibus_max 4000 (stage 3.8 A
plus buck 1.5 A, about 45 W in, 7.6 A into the battery), two flaws:

  - the buck charger share switched on and off every couple of seconds:
    its threshold was on the stage's bus current, which drops by the
    share the buck charger takes over.  Stock compares the current
    from the source, stage and buck charger together;
  - when the pack reached 40 degC and the battery limit fell to 4.5 A,
    the stage dropped from 3.9 A to 0.8 A within 3 s: the gauges
    average over seconds and kept reading 7.3-7.7 A, so the
    proportional step-down on their excess overshot.

Decide the buck charger share on the source's whole current, and hold
the battery limit through the stage's own bus reading: its target is
at most (battery limit - buck charge current) / 2, regulated
proportionally, while a gauge reading above the limit only trims the
request one step a poll.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: hold the warm battery limit for 30 s

Tested with the Xiaomi 120 W adapter: the pack temperature (whole
degrees from the charger firmware) read 39, 40, 39, 38 degC within
four seconds, so the battery limit dropped to 4.5 A and came back, and
the buck charger share went off and on with it, six times in about
four minutes.  The limit itself now steps down smoothly (stage 2.9 A
to 2.2 A towards its 2.0 A target, where it fell to 0.8 A before).

Keep the reduced limit until the battery has been at most 38 degC and
not 40 degC for 30 s.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: trip on a lowered battery limit only once the gauges follow

With the warm limit held for 30 s, the Xiaomi 120 W test at 40 degC
stopped direct charging: the limit fell from 8000 to 4500 mA, the stage
went from 2.87 A to 2.15 A within 4 s (about 4.6 A into the battery),
but the gauges still read 6.9 A when the 5 s grace ran out.  After the
stop they took about 15 s to settle, so they average over 10-15 s.

Let the grace start when the stage has come down to its new target and
make it 30 s.  The stage's own reading holds the limit meanwhile.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: bring the warm battery limit back in steps

With the trip fixed, the Xiaomi 120 W test at 40 degC showed two more
flaws:

  - the gauges kept reading above the lowered limit for 10-15 s, and
    each poll stepped the stage down by another 20 mV meanwhile: it fell
    to 1.1 A on the bus (about 2.6 A into the battery against 4.5 A);
  - the pack reading follows the current within seconds (40 to 37 degC
    in 12 s after the step down, while the gauges read 35 degC), so
    30 s later the limit went back to 8 A and the pack reached 40 degC
    again 40 s after that, a 70 s saw tooth between 36 W and 25 W.

Trim through the gauges only once they had the grace to catch up, and
bring the limit back 500 mA every 15 s after the 30 s hold, so that it
settles below the current that warms the pack to 40 degC.  At 40 degC
it still is the stock 4.5 A.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: try direct charging right after the authentication

A Xiaomi adapter does not reset itself after the authentication, so
direct charging always sat out the whole 30 s reset wait at 5 V 1.5 A
before it started.  Stock starts it right after writing the adapter
verified.

Try it once as soon as the authentication is over (verify_process back
to 0 kicks the poll).  A source that refuses the request, such as the
MiPPS power bank that resets about 15 s after its authentication, goes
back to waiting for that reset as before.  A drop inside the reset
window is that reset, not the source's current limit, and is not
learned.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: start direct charging again after a new authentication

A replug within MCA_CP_DROP_FORGET_MS keeps the adapter verified, so
direct charging starts at once, and the authentication that
xiaomi-mipps-auth runs on every attach then stops it.  It stayed off
until the next detach, leaving the adapter on the 9 V buck charger.

Let it start again once the authentication is over.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

* piano: mca: learn a source's limit from the stage and buck input together

With the buck charger in parallel a MiPPS power bank (5 A APDO, about
3.2 A in practice) dropped out at 1480 mA through the stage plus about
1.7 A through the buck charger.  Only the stage's share was learned, a
980 mA bus limit too low to start the stage again, so the power bank
was left on the 9 V buck charger.

Learn the two together and keep both within it: what the source gives
is its APDO current or the learned limit, whichever is lower, and the
buck charger goes in parallel only if that leaves room for it.

Signed-off-by: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>

